NotesString/You can open this notes window for any project by selecting View->Notes...

This example shows the ISO7816-3 / Smart Card / SIM interpreter decoding the "Answer to
Reset" (ATR) response from a typical Smart Card. In this example the baud rate changes 
on the second response. Two instances of the interpreter have been created so that the 
two different data rates can be interpreted.

Note that this acquisition was limited to ~500ms due to the "Post-Fill Time Limit" setting of
0.5sec (see Setup->Sample Mode...).

A cursor has been place next to each of several points of interest in this captured data. 
From within the Waveforms or State List tabs, you can quickly scroll to cursors A through F 
by pressing the <A> through <F> keys on your keyboard. 

You can quickly zoom in or out by pressing the <+> or <-> keys on the numerical 
keypad of your keyboard. 

By zooming in near each of the cursors, the following sequence can be observed:

At cursor A the TS initial character value of 3Fh (ASCII "?") is transferred. Its value indicates 
"Inverse" convention is being used. Cursor B has been used to measure the start bit rate of 
9.597KHz indicating the standard intial baud rate of 9600. The interpreter has been set 
accordingly.

At cursor C the second transmission begins with TS initial character again 3Fh (ASCII "?"), but 
during this transmission the baud rate has changed. Cursor D has been used to determine the 
baud rate of 14925 and the second interpreter instance has been set accordingly. 

The two interpreter instances can now interpreter data transferred at their respective baud 
rates. Note that each interpreter will indicate parity and guard bit errors during the portion of 
the sequence which does not occur at its specified baud rate.

Please note that all of the example files are "read only" so that they remain intact
for future reference. You can change settings in these files for learning purposes, 
but the changes cannot be saved. You can however use the "Save As" option to 
save an editable copy of any example file.

/
